---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="BulkMagic — Streamlining Multi-State Seller Onboarding" theme="light" includeCaseStudyScript>
<!-- Luminous Gallery Atmosphere: Layered Warm Ambient Gradients -->
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[#FAF9F5]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_75%_55%_at_70%_10%,rgba(217,119,6,0.045),transparent_65%)]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_45%_at_15%_25%,rgba(13,148,136,0.035),transparent_60%)]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_55%_40%_at_85%_75%,rgba(217,119,6,0.03),transparent_70%)]"></div>

<main id="main" class="relative max-w-page mx-auto px-6 md:px-16 lg:px-20 pb-72 pt-20 md:pt-32 font-sans text-neutral-800 selection:bg-amber-500/20 selection:text-neutral-900">

  <!-- HERO SECTION: Grounded Headline & Sprint Scope -->
  <section class="mb-32 md:mb-44">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mb-16">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl sm:text-7xl lg:text-[6.25rem] font-normal leading-[0.94] tracking-[-0.04em] text-neutral-950 mb-10 text-balance">
        Designing Multi-State Merchant Onboarding.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-neutral-800 font-normal leading-snug tracking-tight mb-12 max-w-[50ch]">
        Simplifying legal compliance so new merchants can get approved and start selling, fast.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_0.7fr] gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-start pt-6 border-t border-neutral-200">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl text-neutral-800 font-normal leading-[1.75] max-w-[52ch] text-pretty">
            To get merchants selling quickly, onboarding needs to be painless. In a rapid day-and-a-half sprint, I mapped an adaptive compliance flow that cuts out irrelevant paperwork and built an AI-assisted proof of concept to validate the interaction model.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Margin Ledger: Pure High-Signal Coordinates (Zero Redundancy) -->
        <div class="lg:pt-2 pl-0 lg:pl-10">
          <dl class="space-y-5 text-xs font-mono">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[10px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase mb-1 font-medium">MY ROLE</dt>
              <dd class="text-neutral-950 text-sm font-medium">Product &amp; Interaction Designer</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[10px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase mb-1 font-medium">DELIVERABLES</dt>
              <dd class="text-neutral-950 text-sm font-medium">Compliance Architecture &amp; AI-Generated Prototype</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Hero Mockup Stage: Clean, Honest Presentation (No Fake Chrome) -->
    <figure class="group relative overflow-hidden pt-6 border-t border-neutral-200">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white/95 shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="lightbox-trigger block w-full text-left cursor-zoom-in relative focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600"
          aria-label="Enlarge image: BulkMagic merchant onboarding suite overview"
        >
          <img
            src="/assets/bulkmagic/cover.png"
            alt="BulkMagic merchant onboarding interface suite overview"
            class="w-full h-auto object-contain p-4 sm:p-8 hover:scale-[1.008] transition-luxury duration-700"
            loading="eager"
          />
          <span class="absolute bottom-4 right-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md bg-neutral-950/80 text-white text-xs font-mono opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-200 pointer-events-none backdrop-blur-xs">
            <span>Enlarge ↗</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-4 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-3">
        BulkMagic Merchant Onboarding Suite Overview
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- THE CONSTRAINT -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-y border-neutral-200 mb-28 md:mb-36">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 leading-[1.06] tracking-tight font-normal text-balance">
        42 legal questions stood between a new seller and their first sale.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 font-normal text-lg leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p class="text-neutral-950 font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
          Marketplaces can't bypass compliance. Federal and state laws strictly require verifying identities, collecting W-9 tax forms, and tracking sales tax obligations across every operating jurisdiction. When you compile the full checklist of potential legal requirements across all business entity types, it totals 42 separate questions and filings.
        </p>
        <p>
          Standard compliance portals approach this by presenting all 42 questions as a monolithic form. For a new merchant trying to launch quickly, that creates an immediate wall of legal anxiety.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE DISCOVERY -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-b border-neutral-200 mb-28 md:mb-36">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 leading-[1.06] tracking-tight font-normal text-balance">
        28 of those 42 questions were corporate noise.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 font-normal text-lg leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p class="text-neutral-950 font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
          Auditing the statutory requirements revealed that 67% of the friction was artificial. 28 of the 42 requirements—such as Articles of Incorporation, board resolutions, and complex multi-state nexus forecasts—apply strictly to C-Corps and multi-tier entities.
        </p>
        <p>
          The roadblock wasn’t compliance itself. It was the naive assumption that every seller needed to answer every question.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE ADAPTIVE ARCHITECTURE -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-b border-neutral-200 mb-32 md:mb-40">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6 mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 leading-[1.06] tracking-tight font-normal text-balance">
        Filtering out the noise so sellers finish in minutes, not days.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 font-normal text-lg leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p class="text-neutral-950 font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
          The solution was to make the flow adaptive. Asking two foundational questions first—business structure and location—immediately hides the 28 corporate requirements that don't apply.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pairing dynamic filtering with real-time inline validation cuts the field burden from 42 down to 14 and eliminates 7-day manual review cycles. Sellers fix errors as they type and get approved right away.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Comparative Visual Bars & Feedback Loops -->
    <div class="space-y-12 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-8 max-w-4xl">
      
      <!-- Comparison 1: Input Volume -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-600 font-medium">Form Burden Comparison</span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-amber-800 font-medium">From 42 questions down to 14</span>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3 font-mono text-xs">
          <!-- Full Statutory Scope Bar -->
          <div class="space-y-1.5">
            <div class="flex justify-between text-neutral-700 text-[11px]">
              <span>Exhaustive Legal Checklist (All business types combined)</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-neutral-950">42 Questions</span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-6 w-full rounded bg-neutral-200/80 overflow-hidden flex">
              <div class="h-full bg-neutral-400 w-full flex items-center px-3 text-[10px] text-white font-medium">
                42 Legal Fields (100% Scope)
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- BulkMagic Adaptive Bar -->
          <div class="space-y-1.5 pt-2">
            <div class="flex justify-between text-neutral-700 text-[11px]">
              <span class="text-neutral-950 font-medium">BulkMagic Adaptive Flow (Tailored to seller entity)</span>
              <span class="font-semibold text-amber-800">14 Relevant Fields</span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-6 w-full rounded bg-neutral-200/80 overflow-hidden flex">
              <div class="h-full bg-amber-600 rounded-l w-[33.3%] flex items-center px-3 text-[10px] text-white font-medium shrink-0">
                14 Fields (-67%)
              </div>
              <div class="h-full bg-neutral-100 flex-1 flex items-center px-3 text-[10px] text-neutral-500 font-sans">
                28 corporate-only questions automatically filtered out
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Comparison 2: Error Feedback Cycles -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 pt-4 border-t border-neutral-200">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-neutral-200 pb-2.5">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-600 font-medium">Manual Post-Submission Review</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-neutral-950">7–14 Days Delay</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-400 font-mono text-[11px]">
            <span>Submit form</span>
            <span>→</span>
            <span>Manual compliance audit</span>
            <span>→</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-800 font-medium">Email rejection</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 font-sans leading-relaxed">
            Typo in an EIN or an unreadable certificate triggers an email days later, forcing the seller to recall context and re-upload documents.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-neutral-200 pb-2.5">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-800 font-medium">BulkMagic Inline Check</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-amber-800">Instant (0s Latency)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-800 font-mono text-[11px]">
            <span>Type input</span>
            <span>→</span>
            <span>Syntax &amp; format check</span>
            <span>→</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-950 font-medium">Immediate confirmation</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 font-sans leading-relaxed">
            Field formatting, tax ID syntax, and attachments are verified immediately with clear error prompts while the seller is actively typing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- INTERACTION WALKTHROUGH -->
  <section class="mb-48 md:mb-56">
    <div class="space-y-36 md:space-y-48">

      <!-- ENTITY CLASSIFICATION & ROUTING -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            Setting the Rules Based on Business Structure
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            The first interaction asks two basic questions: what is your business structure, and where do you operate? Answering this upfront sets the rules for the rest of the flow, immediately suppressing 28 corporate tax questions that don't legally apply.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="group">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="lightbox-trigger block w-full text-left cursor-zoom-in relative focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600"
              aria-label="Enlarge image: Business structure identification and entity routing interface"
            >
              <img
                src="/assets/bulkmagic/progressive-disclosure.png"
                alt="Business structure identification and progressive disclosure routing interface"
                class="w-full h-auto object-contain block hover:scale-[1.006] transition-luxury duration-700"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <span class="absolute bottom-4 right-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md bg-neutral-950/80 text-white text-xs font-mono opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-200 pointer-events-none backdrop-blur-xs">
                <span>View Full Resolution ↗</span>
              </span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Step-by-step business structure identification &amp; routing
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <!-- DYNAMIC REQUIREMENTS CHECKLIST -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            An Upfront, Personalized Document Checklist
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            Instead of springing document requests mid-flow, the checklist establishes clear expectations before asking for an upload. Sellers see an upfront time budget (&lt;6 minutes) and the exact files needed (like a W-9 and resale certificate), giving them predictability to finish in one sitting.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="group">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="lightbox-trigger block w-full text-left cursor-zoom-in relative focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600"
              aria-label="Enlarge image: Dynamic document checklist tailored to seller profile"
            >
              <img
                src="/assets/bulkmagic/document-checklist.png"
                alt="Dynamic document checklist adapting in real time to entity type and location"
                class="w-full h-auto object-contain block hover:scale-[1.006] transition-luxury duration-700"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <span class="absolute bottom-4 right-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md bg-neutral-950/80 text-white text-xs font-mono opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-200 pointer-events-none backdrop-blur-xs">
                <span>View Full Resolution ↗</span>
              </span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Dynamic requirements checklist tailored to seller profile
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <!-- AUTOMATED INLINE VALIDATION -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            Catching Errors Inline Rather Than via Email
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            Submitting an application and waiting days only to discover a typo in a tax ID creates instant frustration. Inline validation checks syntax and state nexus rules in real time as the seller types, catching errors when they are easiest to fix.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="group">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="lightbox-trigger block w-full text-left cursor-zoom-in relative focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600"
              aria-label="Enlarge image: Real-time inline syntax validation and error handling"
            >
              <img
                src="/assets/bulkmagic/automated-validation.png"
                alt="Real-time inline syntax validation and economic nexus threshold checks"
                class="w-full h-auto object-contain block hover:scale-[1.006] transition-luxury duration-700"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <span class="absolute bottom-4 right-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md bg-neutral-950/80 text-white text-xs font-mono opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-200 pointer-events-none backdrop-blur-xs">
                <span>View Full Resolution ↗</span>
              </span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Instant error resolution and document validation interface
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <!-- TRANSPARENT REVIEW & ACTIVATION -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            In-Place Edits Before Final Activation
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            A single summary screen confirms registered details, tax nexuses, and bank payout information in a clean ledger. Sellers can edit details directly in place without clicking "back" through multiple screens, leading immediately into active selling.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="group">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="lightbox-trigger block w-full text-left cursor-zoom-in relative focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600"
              aria-label="Enlarge image: Account activation and onboarding success screen"
            >
              <img
                src="/assets/bulkmagic/onboarding-success.png"
                alt="Account activation confirmation and success screen"
                class="w-full h-auto object-contain block hover:scale-[1.006] transition-luxury duration-700"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <span class="absolute bottom-4 right-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md bg-neutral-950/80 text-white text-xs font-mono opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-200 pointer-events-none backdrop-blur-xs">
                <span>View Full Resolution ↗</span>
              </span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Account activation confirmation and live status review
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SPRINT REFLECTION -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-y border-neutral-200 mb-36 md:mb-48">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-tight">
        Rapid prototyping as a compliance stress-test.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base sm:text-lg text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p>
          In a rapid sprint spanning roughly 36 hours, the goal was to take dense statutory regulations and prove that compliance doesn't have to be a multi-week engineering project before you can validate the experience. Using AI to generate a functional prototype allowed me to stress-test state transitions, uncover edge cases, and capture realistic UI states in hours rather than weeks.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-800">
          If moving to a production build, the immediate next steps would be running live usability tests with active multi-state sellers to benchmark time-to-completion, tracking drop-off across the document checklist, and load-testing the tax ID validation endpoints for real-time responsiveness.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER NAVIGATION -->
  <section class="pt-16 border-t border-neutral-200">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-baseline justify-between gap-12 font-mono text-xs">
      <a href="/vitals" class="group flex flex-col gap-2 transition-luxury">
        <span class="text-[10px] tracking-widest uppercase text-neutral-600 group-hover:text-amber-800 font-medium">← PREVIOUS CASE STUDY</span>
        <span class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal text-neutral-950 group-hover:text-amber-800">Vitals: Digital Medical ID</span>
        <span class="font-sans text-xs text-neutral-600 font-normal">Overcoming the 92% drop-off barrier through trust-first onboarding</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/omara" class="group flex flex-col gap-2 sm:text-right transition-luxury">
        <span class="text-[10px] tracking-widest uppercase text-neutral-600 group-hover:text-amber-800 font-medium">NEXT CASE STUDY →</span>
        <span class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal text-neutral-950 group-hover:text-amber-800">Omara: GovTech Systems</span>
        <span class="font-sans text-xs text-neutral-600 font-normal">Caseworker triage portal &amp; agentic design-system verification</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>
